&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are Ocado Group, and we&#39;re bringing world-class automation to online grocery. Our Ocado Smart Platform (OSP) combines cutting-edge robotics, AI, and IoT within our advanced CFCs (Customer Fulfilment Centres). We&#39;ve mastered the single pick, transforming online delivery for our global partners. Join us and be part of a team pushing the boundaries of retail technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-visibility Senior Finance Manager opportunity to embed directly within Ocado’s Executive team, acting as a key financial partner to the Office of the CEO, Legal and Business Integrity, People, and Reward.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working alongside senior leadership -including the Deputy CEO, Chief People Officer, General Counsel, and Head of Reward-you will own core financial processes across Group Operations, driving monthly management reporting, the annual budget cycle, and rolling outlooks while providing strategic decision support, cost-initiative challenge, and cash flow optimisation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting directly to the Head of Group Financial Planning, you will gain invaluable exposure to Group FP&amp;amp;A, Capital Markets, and Investor Relations, while also mentoring a Finance Business Partner to champion consistency and excellence across the Group Ops finance team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being a trusted finance business partner to key Group Operations functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building strong relationships with senior stakeholders, including the Deputy-CEO, Chief People Officer, General Counsel and Head of Reward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leveraging a strong commercial and technical understanding of Ocado’s business to translate business strategy into financial plans through the preparation of Budgets and Outlooks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing strategic financial support to your business partners, helping to identify financial risks with proposed mitigations and evaluating the financial impact of key cost initiatives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring and reporting monthly spend against budget across partnered functions to support the business in delivering positive cash flow, proactively flagging risks and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying opportunities to streamline finance processes and reporting within Group Ops, improving the quality of data and insight delivered to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing support and guidance to the Finance Business Partner covering GTS, helping build consistency of approach across the Group Ops finance business partnering team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified accountant (ACA, ACCA, CIMA or equivalent) with post-qualification experience in an accounting or a finance business partnering role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in building trusted relationships with senior finance and/or non-finance stakeholders, including at Exec or Exec-1 level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial and management reporting skills, including ownership of budgeting and forecasting (Outlook) cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident using financial systems and BI tools (e.g. EPM, Looker or equivalent) and advanced Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High levels of resilience and positivity, with exceptional attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-driven to both begin and complete tasks, comfortable operating with a lean team and ambiguous or evolving scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive drive for continuous improvement and automation to yield process efficiencies and elevate output quality&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting or mentoring more junior finance colleagues (desirable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in supporting our people with meaningful, flexible benefits that prioritise well-being and work-life balance. Here’s a snapshot of what you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time to recharge:&lt;br&gt;25 days annual leave (rising to 27 after 5 years), plus the option to buy more – and 30 days a year to work from anywhere in the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health &amp;amp; wellbeing:&lt;br&gt;Private Medical Insurance from your first month, wellbeing support through specialist apps and EAP, plus Income Protection and Life Assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-first policies:&lt;br&gt;22 weeks paid maternity/primary carer leave and 6 weeks paid paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial support:&lt;br&gt;Pension with employer matching up to 7%, share schemes (Sharesave &amp;amp; BAYE), and interest-free loans for train tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter perks:&lt;br&gt;Cycle to Work Scheme and free shuttle buses to/from Hatfield and Welwyn Garden City stations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exclusive discounts:&lt;br&gt;15% off at Ocado.com with free delivery (starting in your first month).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
